.TH pdfpagecount 1 "05 November 2026"
.SH NAME
pdfpagecount \- count the pages of a PDF by walking its page tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfpagecount
[options]
.RI [ PDF-file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdfpagecount
opens a PDF the way the other Poppler utilities do (repairing a damaged
xref table and trying an empty user password), walks the page tree from the
catalog's /Pages root and prints the number of leaf page objects it reaches.
.PP
The count comes only from document structure. The root /Count entry, the
linearization dictionary, the Info dictionary, XMP metadata and page content
are never used, so a document cannot claim its own page count.
.PP
Kids are classified the way Poppler builds its page list: a kid that is
/Type /Page, or a dictionary without /Kids, is a page; any other dictionary
is an intermediate node; a kid that does not resolve to a dictionary is
skipped. A page referenced from several places counts every time it is
referenced, because Poppler renders it every time.
.PP
On success the only output is one decimal integer followed by a newline.
Diagnostics go to standard error, are fixed strings and never include
document data.
.PP
If
.I PDF-file
is \'-\', the PDF is read from stdin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-max\-pages " number"
Fail with exit code 3 if the tree holds more than
.I number
pages (default 100000).
.TP
.BI \-max\-depth " number"
Fail with exit code 3 if the tree is more than
.I number
levels deep (default 256).
.TP
.B \-claimed
Also print the root /Count entry on a second line, or "none" if it is not
an integer. For diagnostics only; never use it as the page count.
.TP
.B \-v
Print copyright and version information.
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage information.
.RB ( \-help
and
.B \-\-help
are equivalent.) Every long option also accepts a leading double dash.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
0
The page count was printed.
.TP
1
The file could not be opened or is not a repairable PDF.
.TP
2
The file is encrypted and needs a password.
.TP
3
The page count or tree depth exceeds its limit. Nothing is printed on stdout.
.TP
4
The page tree is malformed: no valid /Pages root, a kid that is not an
indirect reference, a /Kids entry that is not an array, a page Poppler
rejects, or a cycle.
.TP
99
Invalid command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdfinfo (1),
.BR pdftotext (1),
.BR pdftoppm (1)
